  "body": "In a whole bunch of places in the CS API and SS API specs, we refer to the \"state at\" an event, which is ambiguous.\r\n\r\nThis creates a lot of confusion for homeserver developers. It would be great to make sure that we always refer to either the \"state before\" (not including changes made by state events) or \"state after\" (including changes made by state events) an event. ",
